      "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nUnder `--quantization modelopt_fp4` with expert parallelism (`--ep > 1`) and a non-flashinfer MoE runner backend (e.g. `--moe-runner-backend triton`), server startup crashes in `process_weights_after_loading` with:\r\n```\r\nRuntimeError: The size of tensor a (384) must match the size of tensor b (24)\r\nat non-singleton dimension 0\r\n```\r\n\r\nReproduces on `nvidia/Kimi-K2.5-NVFP4` with `--tp 16 --ep 16 --moe-runner-backend triton --quantization modelopt_fp4` (384 routed experts, 24 local per rank).\r\n\r\n## Root cause\r\n\r\nIn `ModelOptNvFp4FusedMoEMethod`, `w13_input_scale` and `w2_input_scale` are registered with `_sglang_require_global_experts = True`, so the weight loader brings all `num_experts` (384) scales onto every rank. `process_weights_after_loading` is responsible for reducing them down to the rank's local-expert range.\r\n\r\nThree backend branches exist in that function:\r\n\r\n| branch | reduction | correct under EP? |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `flashinfer_cutlass` / `flashinfer_trtllm` | `.max()` → scalar | yes (scalar broadcasts) |\r\n| `flashinfer_cutedsl` | explicit `_slice_scale` to `[num_local_experts]` | yes |\r\n| else (generic / triton / cutlass) | `.max(dim=-1).values` → `[num_experts]` | **no, never sliced** |\r\n\r\nDownstream in the same function, `w13_weight_scale_2` / `w2_weight_scale_2` are\r\nalready per-local-expert (size `num_local_experts`). The elementwise multiply\r\n`w13_input_scale * w13_weight_scale_2` then sees `[num_experts] × [num_local_experts]`\r\nand raises.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n- `python/sglang/srt/layers/quantization/modelopt_quant.py`\r\n  - In the generic `else` branch of `process_weights_after_loading`, slice `w13_input_scale` and `w2_input_scale` to this rank's local expert range when `moe_ep_size > 1`. Mirrors what `flashinfer_cutedsl` already does via `_slice_scale`.\r\n\r\n## Test plan\r\n\r\n- [ ] Reproduce on GB200 with `nvidia/Kimi-K2.5-NVFP4`:\r\n  ```bash\r\n  python -m sglang.launch_server \\\r\n      --model-path nvidia/Kimi-K2.5-NVFP4 --lora-use-virtual-experts \\\r\n      --tp 16 --ep 16 \\\r\n      --moe-runner-backend triton \\\r\n      --quantization modelopt_fp4 \\\r\n      --mem-fraction-static 0.8 \\\r\n      --cuda-graph-max-bs 1024 \\\r\n      --trust-remote-code \\\r\n      --reasoning-parser kimi_k2 \\\r\n      --tool-call-parser kimi_k2 \\\r\n      --enable-lora \\\r\n      --max-loras-per-batch 2 \\\r\n      --max-lora-rank 32 \\\r\n      --lora-backend triton \\\r\n      --lora-paths kimi_expert_lora_alpha=<path>\r\n  ```",
      "changedFiles": 1,
